+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional due date, a computed `overdue` flag, an `?overdue=` API filter, and a list page that shows both and filters with a „nur überfällige“ checkbox.
+
+**Architecture:** `TodoStore` stores `DueDate` and computes `Overdue` on every read from an injected `TimeProvider` (UTC date). PATCH distinguishes "field missing" from `null` with a small `Optional<T>` struct plus a System.Text.Json converter factory. `Home.razor` reads `Store.List(...)` as before, adding two spans and a bound checkbox.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, ASP.NET Core minimal API, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, xUnit, `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-due-date-design.md` (Ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages (so no `FakeTimeProvider`; tests use their own `TimeProvider` subclass).
+- Validation errors → HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}` (existing middleware in `Program.cs` maps `ValidationException` and `BadHttpRequestException`).
+- "Heute" = `DateOnly.FromDateTime(timeProvider.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime)`.
+- Overdue ⇔ `DueDate is { } d && d < today && !Done`.
+- JSON date format `"yyyy-MM-dd"`; response shape `{"id":1,"title":"A","done":false,"dueDate":"2026-11-20","overdue":false}`, `"dueDate":null` when unset.
+- New UI elements: `data-testid` `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `filter-overdue`. Copy: `fällig dd.MM.yyyy`, `überfällig`, `nur überfällige`. No styling.
+- TDD: failing test first.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. A done todo with a past date — `overdue:false`, excluded from `?overdue=true` (Task 1 test `DoneTodosAreNeverOverdue`).
+2. Due exactly today, and a local time whose UTC date is already the next day — not overdue / uses UTC date (Task 1 test `OverdueUsesTheUtcDate`).
+3. PATCH that only sets `title` or `done` keeps the due date (Task 2 test `PatchWithoutDueDateKeepsIt`).
+4. Malformed dates: `"morgen"`, `"2026-13-01"`, `"2026-11-20T10:00:00"`, `42` → 400 (Task 2 test `RejectsInvalidDueDates`).
+5. `?overdue=abc` → 400, not a 500 or silent "all" (Task 2 test `RejectsAnInvalidOverdueFilter`).
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — due date, overdue, filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`
+- Create: `src/DemoTodo/Optional.cs` (struct only; converter comes in Task 2)
+- Create: `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/FixedTimeProvider.cs`
+- Test: `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces:
+  - `public record Todo(int Id, string Title, bool Done, DateOnly? DueDate = null, bool Overdue = false);`
+  - `public record NewTodo(string? Title, DateOnly? DueDate = null);`
+  - `public record TodoPatch(string? Title, bool? Done, Optional<DateOnly?> DueDate = default);`
+  - `public readonly struct Optional<T> { bool HasValue; T Value; Optional(T value); static implicit operator Optional<T>(T value); }` — `default` = not provided.
+  - `public TodoStore(TimeProvider? time = null)` (null → `TimeProvider.System`).
+  - `public IReadOnlyList<Todo> List(bool? overdue = null)` — null = all.
+  - `Get`/`Add`/`Update` return todos with `Overdue` computed at call time.
+  - Test helper `public sealed class FixedTimeProvider(DateTimeOffset now) : TimeProvider` overriding `GetUtcNow()`.
+
